# Migration Architecture Rules

## Required Components
The project should be organized around these logical components:
- Zendesk connector
- transformation layer
- BoldDesk connector
- mapping persistence layer
- migration orchestration layer
- reconciliation layer
- retry/error handling layer

## Architectural Constraints
- prefer a modular monolith first
- prefer TypeScript / Node.js
- prefer PostgreSQL for mappings, jobs, and audit logs
- use CLI-first administration
- add queues only when needed

## Required Data Concerns
- preserve source IDs
- preserve chronology of replies and internal notes
- explicitly distinguish public vs internal content
- handle attachments as first-class migration entities
- design for idempotency and resumability